      "text": "\n> [!IMPORTANT] This article only applies to Copilot Pro and Copilot Pro+ subscribers on an existing annual plan who remained on legacy premium request-based billing after June 1, 2026.\n\n\n## What changed with Copilot billing?\n\nGitHub changed how Copilot usage is measured and billed.\n\nBefore June 1, 2026, billing was premium request-based: each model interaction cost one **premium request unit** (PRU), and a **multiplier** was applied based on which model you used—more powerful models used more premium requests. Model multipliers are a concept specific to this legacy request-based billing model.\n\nAs of June 1, 2026, GitHub replaced request-based billing with usage-based billing, where the cost of an interaction depends on two things: the **model** and the **number of toke",
